# Commit-hook tooling comes from the repo root flake (devShells.default),
# defined in ./devshell.nix and composed by ./flake.nix. Entering the directory
# installs the hooks, so a fresh clone needs no install step of its own.
#
# Git shares hooks across worktrees, so one `direnv allow` in any worktree of
# this repository arms the gate for all of them.
use flake
